WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.549
Collagen cream does not
replace your collagen.

00:00:02.769 --> 00:00:05.747
Collagen powder does not travel
straight to your face.

00:00:06.097 --> 00:00:07.907
So where does it actually go?

00:00:08.127 --> 00:00:09.322
Stay for the twist.

00:00:09.542 --> 00:00:12.444
23 trials seem to
say the powder works.

00:00:12.664 --> 00:00:14.440
Remove the industry funded ones,

00:00:14.440 --> 00:00:15.772
and watch what happens.

00:00:15.992 --> 00:00:19.509
But first, what actually protects
the collagen you already have?

00:00:19.859 --> 00:00:21.959
Think of your skin
as a building.

00:00:22.179 --> 00:00:24.245
Collagen is the structure inside it.

00:00:24.465 --> 00:00:26.565
It keeps everything firm and upright.

00:00:26.865 --> 00:00:28.816
As we age, collagen production slows.

00:00:29.036 --> 00:00:32.484
And ultraviolet light switches on
enzymes that cut collagen apart.

00:00:32.704 --> 00:00:35.688
The sun runs a demolition
crew. It works weekends.

00:00:35.988 --> 00:00:37.950
Sunscreen is not just about sunburn.

00:00:38.170 --> 00:00:40.394
It draws a boundary
around the building.

00:00:40.614 --> 00:00:43.753
Preserving collagen is usually far
easier than replacing it.

00:00:44.103 --> 00:00:45.103
Now, the cream.

00:00:45.205 --> 00:00:48.734
To pass through skin, a molecule
generally needs to be under

00:00:48.734 --> 00:00:50.193
about 500 daltons.

00:00:50.413 --> 00:00:52.653
Collagen is around 300,000.

00:00:52.873 --> 00:00:55.044
It is not getting
through that door.

00:00:55.344 --> 00:00:58.527
It may still form a
moisturising film on the surface.

00:00:58.747 --> 00:00:59.843
Skin feels smoother.

00:01:00.063 --> 00:01:03.109
But polishing the windows is
not replacing the beams.

00:01:03.459 --> 00:01:04.459
Now, the powder.

00:01:04.558 --> 00:01:08.305
Swallow collagen, and digestion breaks it
into peptides and amino acids.

00:01:08.525 --> 00:01:10.871
Your stomach does not
offer facial delivery.

00:01:11.171 --> 00:01:12.776
Some pieces may be absorbed.

00:01:12.996 --> 00:01:15.305
Certain peptides may even
act as signals.

00:01:15.525 --> 00:01:17.666
But your body decides
where they go.

00:01:17.886 --> 00:01:20.730
Skin, joints, tendons, wherever
repairs are most urgent.

00:01:20.950 --> 00:01:22.489
Your face ordered scaffolding.

00:01:22.709 --> 00:01:24.582
It got a box
of spare parts.

00:01:25.132 --> 00:01:26.297
Does the powder work?

00:01:26.517 --> 00:01:28.972
Trials do report modest
improvements in hydration,

00:01:28.972 --> 00:01:30.074
elasticity, or wrinkles.

00:01:30.374 --> 00:01:32.039
But many were small, short,

00:01:32.039 --> 00:01:33.197
and industry funded.

00:01:33.497 --> 00:01:36.988
In 2025, researchers pooled
23 randomised trials.

00:01:37.208 --> 00:01:38.423
All together, a benefit.

00:01:38.643 --> 00:01:40.981
Keep only the studies
without industry funding,

00:01:40.981 --> 00:01:43.287
and it is no
longer statistically significant.

00:01:43.507 --> 00:01:46.252
Keep only the higher
quality studies. Same result.

00:01:46.472 --> 00:01:47.968
The effect stops showing up.

00:01:48.268 --> 00:01:49.626
Do supplements definitely work?

00:01:49.846 --> 00:01:51.771
We cannot say that. Definitely fail?

00:01:51.991 --> 00:01:53.783
We cannot confidently say that either.

00:01:54.003 --> 00:01:55.679
The independent evidence is uncertain.

00:01:56.229 --> 00:01:57.940
What the evidence actually supports.

00:01:58.160 --> 00:02:00.670
Broad spectrum sunscreen, every
day. Not smoking.

00:02:00.890 --> 00:02:02.387
Enough protein and vitamin C.

00:02:02.607 --> 00:02:06.149
And for suitable users, topical retinoids
have far stronger evidence for

00:02:06.149 --> 00:02:07.524
collagen than collagen cream.

00:02:07.824 --> 00:02:09.791
Collagen cream is a pleasant moisturiser.

00:02:10.011 --> 00:02:11.343
Collagen powder is optional.

00:02:11.563 --> 00:02:14.529
Protect the building before you
buy expensive powdered bricks.
